have Auspex, Fortitude, Oblivion, same as ever; the Giovanni bloodline (if using the rule that gives them a separate discipline spread) has Dominate, Fortitude, Oblivion. And at the risk of stating the obvious, Presence doesn't necessarily have anything to do with fucking; ever since their first introduction, the True Brujah (the bloodline of cold, emotionless scholars) has had in-clan Presence.<br /> <br /> You're correct that the Giovanni spread was changed in V5, but they gained Fortitude, not Auspex. (Which means that the main Hecata disciplines can be written concisely as Oblivion, Fortitude, Dominate|Auspex|Obfuscate depending on bloodline.) Which kills two birds with one stone, making them closer to the Cappadocians and farther from the Lasombra at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T18:18:14-07:00","id":1395189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395180#post1395180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, OK. I guess the wiki needs to be updated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they need to be related by Blood but if 