u-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T22:31:10-07:00","id":1395243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395115#post1395115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I agree with you on that one. In my games they have a different universal bane, and the agonizing bite is a Flaw you can purchase at chargen like the others.<br /> <br /> What would you have gone with, for a universal bane (since V5's design philosophy means they need one)? For mechanical reasons, some part of it has to scale with &amp;quot;Bane Severity&amp;quot;, but that part can be pretty minor relative to the whole. (The main part of the Tremere bane is they can't blood-bond vampires, for example; the scaling part is that it takes (3+Bane Severity) drinks to bond a mortal, which is much less relevant.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The classic Cappadocian being cold, pale and off putting, not being able to blush of life would have been the big one, the minor part would have been social penalties due to Aura of creepiness (so penalties to seduce, befriend etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T02:30:08-07:00","id":1395271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395220#post1395220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on whether you think the Aralu are Antediluvians or not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Then potentially four.</div> </div> </div> </div>The notion the Aralu were diablerized by the Nagaraja was never introduced or even hinted anywhere. It was said they might be the shades of 3 antediluvians but I always felt their number and description closely matched the second generation.<br /> <br /> In my old Chronicle of Ages the three shades that are sometimes seen among their tombs belong to Enoch, Zillah and Irad, while the empty tomb belongs to Caine himself who was the one who actually brought the second generation's ghosts to Enoch (which in my games is a fragment of the First City from the previous iteration of reality, before th war between Lucifer and the Heavenly Host had ended). Also I had the Lady of Fate from WtO search for the &quot;missing&quot; Aralu for... familial reasons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T02:44:40-07:00","id":1395274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395271#post1395271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The notion the Aralu were diablerized by the Nagaraja was never introduced or even hinted anywhere. It was said they might be the shades of 3 antediluvians but I always felt their number and description closely matched the second generation.<br /> <br /> In my old Chronicle of Ages the three shades that are sometimes seen among their tombs belong to Enoch, Zillah and Irad, while the empty tomb belongs to Caine himself who was the one who actually brought the second generation's ghosts to Enoch (which in my games is a fragment of the First City from the previous iteration of reality, before th war between Lucifer and the Heavenly Host had ended). Also I had the Lady of Fate from WtO search for the &quot;missing&quot; Aralu for... familial reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize I was making a joke comment to a joke, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:17:31-07:00","id":1395283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395274#post1395274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You realize I was making a joke comment to a joke, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously I did not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T04:52:30-07:00","id":1395301,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Nagaraja, Giovanni, and Tremere are all three clans of wizard-vampires who became immortal via the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Two of them ate their Antediluvian but not quite what I meant when I said they were the same.<br /> <br /> My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:03:10-07:00","id":1395306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395301#post1395301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Nagaraja, Giovanni, and Tremere are all three clans of wizard-vampires who became immortal via the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Two of them ate their Antediluvian but not quite what I meant when I said they were the same.<br /> <br /> My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere and the Nagaraja were mortal mages (respectively founding members of the Order of Hermes and a small subsect of the proto-Eutanatoi Chakravanti mages, called the Idran) who found a way to manipolate vampire blood turning themselves into vampires without needing the embrace.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni on the other hand were a family (or according to DAV20 a sort of business/criminal enterprise between likeminded young people) of renowned necromancers and traders who Cappadocius wanted to include into his clan for their knowledge of Necromancy. Augustus Giovanni accepted the offer of the embrace by the eldest Cappadocian himself and his bloodline was thus created by &quot;normal&quot; kindred means via the embrace.<br /> <br /> Edit: as for the Antediluvians and diablerie. Tremere diablerized Saulot, lowered his generation but then realized Sauolt allowed this and was trying to devour his soul and take control of his House for yet undisclosed reasons. Therefore the attempt at diablerie was not completely successfull. Tremere fled his own body at the end of the 20th century but might again be thrid generation due to a ritual he enacted by sacrificing the whole of the Tremere antitribu.<br /> <br /> Augustus Giovanni was allowed to diablerize Cappadocius because the latter vampire believed itwas a necessary part of a ritual he was trying to enact to &quot;diablerize God&quot;. Cappadocius failed, Augustus Giovanni became a 3rd generation vampire BUT he did not consume the ancient's soul. It instead became a wraith and after a few centuries a spectre. This left Augustus as a Vampire with the potential of a 3rd generation vampire WITHOUT the knowledge of an antediluvian. Again the diablerie attempt was only partially successfull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 06-09-2020, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:21:16-07:00","id":1395312,"title":"","content":"Where do the Capadocians have presence? <br /> <br /> It really, really, really doesn't suit them. <br /> <br /> The whole Giovanni eats the capadocians is really allegory for how well organized aggressive capitalists can defeat a lot of complacent, inoffensive, old fashioned competitors in their field. Big business taking on out-of-touch traditionalists. It'd be weird for those no-connections corpse people to have presence. They're not meant to be likeable. <br /> <br /> Fortitude, Auspex and necromancy were excellent at defining the Capadocians. If I had to replace a discipline of theirs, I'd pick obfuscate. Potence and Dominate, meanwhile, were <i>perfect </i>for the Giovanni, even if it makes them lasombra clones, it fits them wonderfully (The potence compensates for the clan weakness, it also shows them as aggressive, Dominate is just the perfect social discipline for how they run things)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T07:39:31-07:00","id":1395592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395115#post1395115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I agree with you on that one. In my games they have a different universal bane, and the agonizing bite is a Flaw you can purchase at chargen like the others.<br /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>For my homebrew, at least, I like the bane, since it adds to the intimidation feel. But yeah it feels weird having all of the Hecata bloodlines have all the same bane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395218#post1395218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which Ante did they diablerize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly implied the Capuchin ambushed Augustus and had a nibble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395312#post1395312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do the Capadocians have presence?<br /> <br /> It really, really, really doesn't suit them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the first post and my second post for my reasoning's on giving them Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","user":"Kahnabys","date":". 06-10-2020, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T11:56:35-07:00","id":1395635,"title":"","content":"I'd give Cappadocians Auspex, Fortitude, and Oblivion.<br /> <br /> But I like how they have a mix of Bloodlines now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:01:13-07:00","id":1395655,"title":"","content":"Ok. I read your second post. <br /> <br /> I don't agree with it. <br /> Presence for fear is, well, not a good thing for a vampire predator to live off. Fear-presence is useful, but it's not core-clan-discipline useful. Making yourself loved is good for feeding. Making people want to avoid you isn't. If you want to feed through fear: Dominate. Easy-as. A vampire using presence for love is smart, a vampire using presence for fear and love is cool, a vampire who uses it only for fear... just use dominate. Getting some fear power might be good as an out-of-clan when your main feeding concerns are covered by your in-clans. <br /> <br /> Also you can be totally scary through mundane means, you don't need a supernatural augmentation to your fear factor when you're legit terrifying without that crutch. <br /> <br /> Auspex, meanwhile, is the choice of an intellectual. It is an excellent choice for a necromancer; finding fetters with strong resonances, finding places filled with ghosts (ghostly eyes causes problems in VTM) and it's kinda good in sneaking around (Knowing there's a person around the corner who could see you when you conduct your ritual is a useful power to have)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T19:24:09-07:00","id":1395726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395655#post1395655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. I read your second post.<br /> <br /> I don't agree with it.<br /> Presence for fear is, well, not a good thing for a vampire predator to live off. Fear-presence is useful...</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, I wasn't clear in my last post, Presence was added not just for the intimidation/fear abilities it gives. Presence, as a discipline, is based on emotion. Changing from Auspex to Presence is the representation of their fury at Lazarus (The Capuchin). It was also easy for them to learn when joining the Anarchs (from The Ministry/Brujah). They went from being scholars to just being... mad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395655#post1395655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to feed through fear: Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the Giovanni and the Nagaraja have Dominate as optional disciplines. I wanted something different and iirc no clan or bloodline has Presence and Necromancy (Oblivion).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395635#post1395635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd give Cappadocians Auspex, Fortitude, and Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395655#post1395655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Auspex) it is an excellent choice for a necromancer; finding fetters with strong resonances, finding places filled with ghosts</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex is still the default if you do not use the optional rules. I agree, but this bloodline is more concerned with reanimating the dead, and not dealing with ghosts (the third bloodline skill gives a bonus to reanimating the dead ceremonies).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also to anyone that's just skipped to the end here, we're discussing my homebrew that's posted in the first comment. My question still remains, would any remnant cappadocian ever go to the camarilla after they sanctioned their destruction through non-interference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","user":"Kahnabys","date":". 06-10-2020, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T19:25:42-07:00","id":1395727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395177#post1395177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nagaraja originally joined the Green Courts anyway so they were always leaving the True Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was in Revised when the True Hand went kablooey and the Nagaraja who were on the living side of the Shroud at the time had to seek shelter somewhere pretty fast to continue existing.<br /> <br /> If the Hand still exists in V5, it's not a given that the Nagaraja would have left it. Certainly a possibility that they and the Harbingers noped out with a communal &quot;There goes the neighborhood!&quot; when the Baali presence became widely known, as you say. But in V20 that was presented as something that had been going on for some time, and I can't imagine the bloodline was okayed for induction as opposed to the standard kill-on-sight treatment without at least the tacit approval of Enoch's Liches and perhaps the Nagaraja Quadi.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T19:32:19-07:00","id":1395729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395727#post1395727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was in Revised when the True Hand went kablooey and the Nagaraja who were on the living side of the Shroud at the time had to seek shelter somewhere pretty fast to continue existing.<br /> <br /> If the Hand still exists in V5, it's not a given that the Nagaraja would have left it. Certainly a possibility that they and the Harbingers noped out with a communal &quot;There goes the neighborhood!&quot; when the Baali presence became widely known, as you say. But in V20 that was presented as something that had been going on for some time, and I can't imagine the bloodline was okayed for induction as opposed to the standard kill-on-sight treatment without at least the tacit approval of Enoch's Liches and perhaps the Nagaraja Quadi.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though we do know that both the Harbingers and Nagaraja went on their own to form the Hecata Blood Cult that just so happened to have eliminated Augustus Giovanni as well as a substantial chunk of his immediate cohorts.<br /> <br /> They might still be members of the True Hand in good standing since said action is hardly against the Tal'Mah'Ra's stated principles. Indeed, killing an Antediluvian killer is a big accomplishment in their eyes, but we know the Harbingers were just humoring the Antediluvian worshipers in the first place.<br /> <br /> I also think Enoch is still destroyed in V5 since the Week of Nightmares happened. It's just the True Hand bounced back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T19:54:46-07:00","id":1395734,"title":"","content":"Hmm, if that's the case it'd have to have had an almost clean sweep of top-level leadership, wouldn't it? I would assume that the Del'Roh and all the wazirs except Izhim ur-Baal and Djuhah would have been annihilated, along with the majority of the Nagaraja bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T20:06:41-07:00","id":1395737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395734#post1395734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, if that's the case it'd have to have had an almost clean sweep of top-level leadership, wouldn't it? I would assume that the Del'Roh and all the wazirs except Izhim ur-Baal and Djuhah would have been annihilated, along with the majority of the Nagaraja bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of things which would have affected the True Hand:<br /> <br /> * The Camarilla no longer persecuting Noddists.<br /> * The Gehenna War<br /> * The fact a shit ton of Ancients are waking up in the Middle East<br /> * Ur-Shulgi pretty much repudiates the Antediluvians are one big happy family<br /> * Jalan and his plan to purge them from the Sabbat is a failure because, well, the Second Inquisition gets him.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T21:03:23-07:00","id":1395752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kahnabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395726#post1395726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also to anyone that's just skipped to the end here, we're discussing my homebrew that's posted in the first comment. My question still remains, would any remnant cappadocian ever go to the camarilla after they sanctioned their destruction through non-interference?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure <i>some</i> would, just because the Cappadocians are a large and diverse clan, and if e.g. some Harbinger was on the run after betraying the Sabbat, the Camarilla might look really appealing.<br /> <br /> But never a large contingent; I'm pretty sure the wiki is just downright wrong about that. I haven't been able to find any support for that idea in <i>Cults</i>, the only place Cappadocians have appeared so far in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T21:06:06-07:00","id":1395754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395727#post1395727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was in Revised when the True Hand went kablooey and the Nagaraja who were on the living side of the Shroud at the time had to seek shelter somewhere pretty fast to continue existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we know a lot of Nagaraja ended up losing their former allegiances and looking for new allies in strange places (and also that the Week of Nightmares happened), I'm assuming Enoch still got blown up in the V5 timeline. It's implied that their joining up with the Hecata is less because of any particular <i>liking</i> for the Giovanni or Cappas, and more because &quot;any port in a storm&quot; (or, in this case, a Maelstrom), and I can't really imagine that happening if Enoch still existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T21:06:11-07:00","id":1395755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395752#post1395752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure <i>some</i> would, just because the Cappadocians are a large and diverse clan, and if e.g. some Harbinger was on the run after betraying the Sabbat, the Camarilla might look really appealing.<br /> <br /> But never a large contingent; I'm pretty sure the wiki is just downright wrong about that. I haven't been able to find any support for that idea in <i>Cults</i>, the only place Cappadocians have appeared so far in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hecata have their own power base now after all. All the Giovanni's former wealth and several bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T00:30:13-07:00","id":1395780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395752#post1395752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure <i>some</i> would, just because the Cappadocians are a large and diverse clan, and if e.g. some Harbinger was on the run after betraying the Sabbat, the Camarilla might look really appealing.<br /> <br /> But never a large contingent; I'm pretty sure the wiki is just downright wrong about that. I haven't been able to find any support for that idea in <i>Cults</i>, the only place Cappadocians have appeared so far in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I first wrote this homebrew I thought the answer was hell no. But the more I hear, I'm now leaning towards probably hell no, lol.<br /> <br /> Lorewise- I can understand a few remnants having old Ventrue homies, so they'd join the Camarilla. But for the majority being a Hecata would be horrifying.<br /> <br /> Lazarus, is not the savior of the clan. He didn't try to save those condemned to death until after they were condemned to death. Now he owns the Harbingers out of gratitude. The ritual he used to unite the clan had to have had the True Vessel, how else would all in the clan of death change, besides if he used Cappadocius' blood? Lazarus, betrayed the Cappadocian's for power. Cappadocius, betrayed his clan for power. The true Cappadocian's are dust. But maybe a few survived? Where would they go? The Camarilla sanctioned their destruction. The Harbingers surely have contacts in the Sabbat. You're breaking away from the only independent... they joined the Anarchs because multiple times Lazarus could have saved the clan, but he only saved himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","user":"Kahnabys","date":". 06-11-2020, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T00:44:39-07:00","id":1395784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kahnabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395726#post1395726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My bad, I wasn't clear in my last post, Presence was added not just for the intimidation/fear abilities it gives. Presence, as a discipline, is based on emotion. Changing from Auspex to Presence is the representation of their fury at Lazarus (The Capuchin). It was also easy for them to learn when joining the Anarchs (from The Ministry/Brujah). They went from being scholars to just being... mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being emotional just doesn't give you presence. Otherwise the malkavains would have presence, and they don't. Salubri also never developed presence despite being really, really mad. Vampire clans develop clan specific disciplines because of their feeding strategies and how they live. The Capadocian lifestyle is not conducive to Presence at all. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Auspex is still the default if you do not use the optional rules. I agree, but this bloodline is more concerned with reanimating the dead, and not dealing with ghosts (the third bloodline skill gives a bonus to reanimating the dead ceremonies). </div> </div> </div>Ironically I believe presence is still actually useful when dealing with ghosts, but it is entirely useless with reanimated corpses. You've taken a weird angle here. Especially because re-animating the dead is generally the repulsive hobby of someone who doesn't make friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T01:05:54-07:00","id":1395786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395784#post1395784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being emotional just doesn't give you presence. Otherwise the malkavains would have presence, and they don't. Salubri also never developed presence despite being really, really mad. Vampire clans develop clan specific disciplines because of their feeding strategies and how they live. The Capadocian lifestyle is not conducive to Presence at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, Auspex is the default, if the optional rule isn't used.<br /> <br /> But even by your reasoning, you don't think more would survive in an Anarch domain if they had Presence over Auspex? You're still thinking of these Cappadocian's from their old clan, these are Cappadocian's the Hecata bloodline. Changed by the Lazarus ritual.<br /> <br /> Also Salubri Antitribu had Valeran instead of Obeah, seems like an angry change to me (yes, I know it's a bastardization of the warrior caste). The Malkavian's went from Dominate to Dementation, seems like crazy change to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395784#post1395784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically I believe presence is still actually useful when dealing with ghosts, but it is entirely useless with reanimated corpses. You've taken a weird angle here. Especially because re-animating the dead is generally the repulsive hobby of someone who doesn't make friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pisanob already have a ghost related ceremony boon ability. Mortis did not have any ghost abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","user":"Kahnabys","date":". 06-11-2020, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T02:37:54-07:00","id":1395796,"title":"","content":"It'd work well if they acted as likeable folks who used presence to charm the pants off of people, though that would neccessitate a different weakness (At which point are you even dealing with Capadocians?) Being &quot;spooky&quot; with presence is not a better survival strat than just having another discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T02:48:44-07:00","id":1395798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395796#post1395796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd work well if they acted as likeable folks who used presence to charm the pants off of people, though that would neccessitate a different weakness (At which point are you even dealing with Capadocians?) Being &quot;spooky&quot; with presence is not a better survival strat than just having another discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue being able to scare away attackers or people mettling has its merits too. As a Hecata bloodline they already have the bane of a painful kiss. I think we might have to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T03:34:27-07:00","id":1395802,"title":"","content":"If they have a painful kiss they want dominate, obfuscate or potence. Animalism might be of service. presence would be your worst bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T10:58:29-07:00","id":1395862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395802#post1395802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have a painful kiss</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, all Hecata bloodlines in V5 have the same bane.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kahnabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395798#post1395798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we might have to agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395802#post1395802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...they want dominate, obfuscate or potence. Animalism might be of service. presence would be your worst bet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I'm going to say this slowly since your reading comprehension is trash, as I have already said 2 Hecata bloodlines have Dominate. The Samedi have Obfuscate. The Lamia have Potence. No clan or bloodline has Presence and Necromancy (Oblivion). Logically they were most exposed to Presence in the Anarchs and it matches their fury they are feeling. So I will state this plainly, I don't care if that doesn't fit your view of what a Cappadocian is or what would be better for hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","user":"Kahnabys","date":".  formatting and clarity 06-11-2020, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T11:45:34-07:00","id":1395870,"title":"","content":"Look, if you've got an idea you like and want to run, go for it. But don't get upset when others don't like your idea. If you don't want to discuss things, you're in the wrong place. I read perfectly fine your ideas and justifications for it; They're <i>bad. </i>How is it that &quot;Logically they were most exposed to Presence in the Anarchs and it matches their fury and feeling&quot;. Like, what? What part of that is logical? the the latter part sounds like one of those in-flight shopping catalogs trying to sell product at the airport. <br /> <br /> Have you, perchance, read material pre-V5? Gio: Potence,Dominate,Necromancy. Capa: Fortitude, Auspex, Necromancy. Sam: Fortitude, Obfuscate, Thanatosis. Lamia (who're extinct) Potence, Necromancy, Fortitude, Nagaraja have Auspex, dominate and necromancy. <br /> <br /> Necromancers having never had Presence as an in-clan discipline is not &quot;free real estate&quot;, it's a deliberate artistic move. Necromancy is a discipline for weirdos who don't make friends and are statistically more likely to fuck a corpse than a living person. Every single necromancer bloodline has had weaknesses that socially ostracise them (Immense pain bite, Corpse look, Rotting corpse look, disease bite, mandatory cannibalism with freaky teeth) . If you want to ignore that, do as you like (or as your storyteller allows) but don't cry when someone points out your idea doesn't fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T11:47:17-07:00","id":1395871,"title":"","content":"Cappadocians having Presence doesn't really work for me because their flaw is essentially, &quot;We are kind of repulsive corpse creatures. Except Serena.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T11:50:02-07:00","id":1395872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395871#post1395871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cappadocians having Presence doesn't really work for me because their flaw is essentially, &quot;We are kind of repulsive corpse creatures. Except Serena.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Hecata bloodline they are not &quot;repulsive corpse creatures&quot; they have the Giovanni's painful kiss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T11:57:43-07:00","id":1395873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kahnabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395862#post1395862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I'm going to say this slowly since your reading comprehension is trash...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice way to get everyone to ignore you by starting out like that.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll reply anyway though with the observation that not every bloodline has (or needs) its own unique discipline spread.<br /> <br /> Even in V20 the Harbingers and Cappadocians had identical discipline spreads. Likewise the Mariner bloodline of Gangrel have the exact same spread as mainline Gangrels (while City Gangrel have a different spread) and the Wu Zao can have the disciplines of either the mainline or antitribu Salubri.<br /> <br /> Presence for Cappadocians doesn\u2019t make a lot of sense for their history and normal predilections and accusing anyone who disagreeing with of being too stupid to read (vs. just not agreeing with you) is a poor debate tactic that is unlikely to convince anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T11:59:37-07:00","id":1395874,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395870#post1395870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/I]How is it that &quot;Logically they were most exposed to Presence in the Anarchs and it matches their fury and feeling&quot;. Like, what? What part of that is logical? the the latter part sounds like one of those in-flight shopping catalogs trying to sell product at the airport.</div> </div> </div> </div>They joined the Anarchs. The Anarchs have the Ministry and the Brujah. Both of those clans have Presence. Meaning they would have more of a chance to learn it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395870#post1395870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But don't get upset when others don't like your idea. If you don't want to discuss things, you're in the wrong place. I read perfectly fine your ideas and justifications for it; They're <i>bad. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. I have provided my reason why they went with Presence and I disagree they are &quot;bad&quot;, I believe you think they are &quot;bad&quot; because you are stuck on what the Cappadocians were and not what this bloodline is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:01:25-07:00","id":1395875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kahnabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395872#post1395872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a Hecata bloodline they are not &quot;repulsive corpse creatures&quot; they have the Giovanni's painful kiss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but that's still part of their history and the Painful Kiss means Presence is pretty useless for feeding.<br /> <br /> I love Presence as a discipline and like seductive monsters but the Cappadocians get nerfed stat wise by Painful Kiss + Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-11-2020, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:01:45-07:00","id":1395876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395873#post1395873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice way to get everyone to ignore you by starting out like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, my bad, it is frustrating repeating what I have already justified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:06:08-07:00","id":1395878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395875#post1395875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes but that's still part of their history and the Painful Kiss means Presence is pretty useless for feeding.<br /> <br /> I love Presence as a discipline and like seductive monsters but the Cappadocians get nerfed stat wise by Painful Kiss + Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 Presence has intimidation/fear abilities which is where I was going with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:08:08-07:00","id":1395880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kahnabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395874#post1395874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't agree. I have provided my reason why they went with Presence and I disagree they are &quot;bad&quot;, I believe you think they are &quot;bad&quot; because you are stuck on what the Cappadocians were and not what this bloodline is.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're necromancers now, necromancers tomorrow, necromancers... wait.<br /> Basically, so long as they're necromancers with the banes they have, they're not likely to pick up presence. Practicing magic isn't a social activity. Practicing necromancy is even less. <br /> <br /> If they want to pick up Presence Out-of-Clan from anarchs, fine. But they're not going to replace a clan discipline because they know Brujah and settites now. I mean, the anarchs literally have every clan among their ranks and they haven't all homogonized into Toreador.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-11-2020, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:10:45-07:00","id":1395881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395880#post1395880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're necromancers now, necromancers tomorrow, necromancers... wait.<br /> Basically, so long as they're necromancers with the banes they have, they're not likely to pick up presence.<br /> <br /> If they want to pick up Presence Out-of-Clan from anarchs, fine. But they're not going to replace a clan discipline because they know Brujah and settites now. I mean, the anarchs literally have every clan among their ranks and they haven't all homogonized into Toreador.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lazarus ritual changed them which manifested as the optional discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:12:05-07:00","id":1395882,"title":"","content":"Hear me out for a moment: <br /> <br /> All the freaky social shit you want them to do can be done with oblivion. Presence is redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:15:25-07:00","id":1395883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kahnabys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395798#post1395798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we might have to agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394746-v5-cappadocians?p=1395882#post1395882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hear me out for a moment:<br /> <br /> All the freaky social shit you want them to do can be done with oblivion. Presence is redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touche, but they didn't, they learned Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:05:07-07:00","id":1395893,"title":"","content":"They sound a bit like blunt Harbingers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T04:47:13-07:00","id":1396646,"title":"","content":"Adding Presence to Cappadocians is an interesting concept. I wouldn't go with it myself, but it's definitely a fun thought experiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}